**What version are you using?**
v1.5.0

**What did you do?**
Set `"indent": 2` in my config, and ran `eslint --fix` on a file with incorrect indentation:

```
function foo(){
   alert('3 spaces!');
   (function () {
     alert('nested indentation');
   })();
}
```

**What happened?**
Running eslint without `--fix` produces the following, as expected:

```
2:4  error  Expected indentation of 4 space characters but found 3  indent
3:4  error  Expected indentation of 4 space characters but found 3  indent
4:6  error  Expected indentation of 7 space characters but found 5  indent

✖ 3 problems (3 errors, 0 warnings)
```

but running with `--fix` only partially fixed the indentation:

```
function foo(){
    alert('3 spaces!');
    (function () {
       alert('nested indentation');
   })();
}
```

Running eslint again without `--fix` confirms the file still has indentation issues:

```
4:8  error  Expected indentation of 8 space characters but found 7  indent
5:4  error  Expected indentation of 4 space characters but found 3  indent

✖ 2 problems (2 errors, 0 warnings)
```

**What did you expect to happen?**
The file should be fully fixed according to the specified indentation (4 spaces), and further runs of `eslint` on the file should pass cleanly.

Expected file after `eslint --fix`:

```
function foo(){
    alert('3 spaces!');
    (function () {
        alert('nested indentation');
    })();
}
```

v2.0.0-beta.2

I tried to migrate from https://github.com/nodeca/eslint-plugin-nodeca and found one problem.

The following code:

``` js
/* eslint indent: [2, 2] */

foo.bar()
   .baz(function () {

  var a;
  // function body
});


foo.bar(
    baz,
    baq,
    function () {

  var a;
  // function body
});
```

give this errors:

```
   6:3  error  Expected indentation of 5 space characters but found 2  indent
   8:1  error  Expected indentation of 3 space characters but found 0  indent
  16:3  error  Expected indentation of 6 space characters but found 2  indent
  18:1  error  Expected indentation of 4 space characters but found 0  indent
```

I expect no errors. See real code sample: https://github.com/nodeca/nodeca.core/blob/master/lib/autoload/hooks/init/faye.js#L240-L249
